# Flutter Build Verification

## Always Build Before Deploying

After editing any `.dart` file, run `flutter build web --release` locally before deploying. If the build fails, fix ALL errors before deploying — do not deploy a stale build.

## Capture Errors Efficiently

```bash
cd mobile && flutter build web --release 2>&1 | grep -E "^lib/|Error:|error:" | head -30
```

## Known Widget Field Mismatches (Do Not Repeat)

| Widget | Correct Field | Wrong Field |
|---|---|---|
| `CoachDashboardScreenV2` | `widget.currentUserProfile` | `widget.profile` |
| `CommunityMeshScreen` | `profile` only (no `token` param) | `profile` + `token` |
| `AppConfig` | `AppConfig.apiBaseUrl` | `AppConfig.apiUrl` (does not exist) |

## Design Token Completeness

The `_Design` class in `settings_screen.dart` must include all color tokens from the design system. If code references a missing token, add it — don't remove the reference.

| Token | Value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `goldDim` | `Color(0xFF8B7355)` | Was missing, caused build failure |

## Deploy Sequence

1. Edit `.dart` files
2. Run `flutter build web --release` — must succeed
3. `rsync -avz mobile/build/web/ root@68.183.168.75:/var/www/sovereignsanctuary-web/` (no `--delete`)
4. `rsync -avz mobile/build/web/ root@68.183.168.75:/var/www/coach-portal/` (no `--delete`)
5. Verify `flutter_bootstrap.js` in deployed `index.html`
6. Verify no-cache headers on service worker
